{"tool_name":"metavisitor","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"metavisitor","home":"https://github.com/ARTbio/metavisitor","summary":"Software package that allows biologists and clinicians without specialized bioinformatics expertise to detect and assemble viral genomes from deep sequence datasets.","addition_date":"2018-06-02T07:43:28Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:02:44.785436Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application"],"collections":["Galaxy"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:metavisitor","credit":[{"email":"christophe.antoniewski@upmc.fr","name":"Christophe Antoniewski","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://artbio.github.io/Metavisitor-manual/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["Naira"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0292"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"Metavisitor","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"migle_sur","publication":[{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0168397","metadata":{"abstract":"Metavisitor is a software package that allows biologists and clinicians without specialized bioinformatics expertise to detect and assemble viral genomes from deep sequence datasets. The package is composed of a set of modular bioinformatic tools and workflows that are implemented in the Galaxy framework. Using the graphical Galaxy workflow editor, users with minimal computational skills can use existing Metavisitor workflows or adapt them to suit specific needs by adding or modifying analysis modules. Metavisitor works with DNA, RNA or small RNA sequencing data over a range of read lengths and can use a combination of de novo and guided approaches to assemble genomes from sequencing reads. We show that the software has the potential for quick diagnosis as well as discovery of viruses from a vast array 